cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Forma, please cite the companion paper and, where relevant, the published weight and forecast artifacts."
title: "Forma: A Tuple-Set Transformer Pro-Forma Financial Statement Forecaster"
abstract: >-
  Forma is a tuple-set Transformer that jointly forecasts the complete quarterly
  financial statements of U.S. public firms at horizons of 1 to 20 quarters,
  emitting a predictive distribution per statement item. This repository ships
  the model code and the configurations for Forma and every competitor in the
  ProForma-20Q benchmark. It contains source code and configuration only: the
  trained Forma checkpoints -- five seeds each for the Gaussian and Laplace
  families -- are published separately on the Hugging Face Hub under a
  non-commercial research licence, and the Apache-2.0 licence here does not
  extend to them. It ships no data; real-data reproduction uses the companion
  ProForma-20Q package and WRDS credentials.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/forma-lab-mccombs/forma-release"
url: "https://github.com/forma-lab-mccombs/forma-release"
keywords:
  - financial-statement-forecasting
  - probabilistic-forecasting
  - tuple-set-transformer
  - proforma-20q
  - Compustat
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://huggingface.co/forma-lab-mccombs/forma"
    description: >-
      Trained Forma checkpoints (five seeds each for the Gaussian and Laplace
      families), under the Forma Non-Commercial Research Licence v1.0.
  - type: url
    value: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/forma-lab-mccombs/proforma-20q-artifacts"
    description: >-
      Canonical Forma forecast parquets, the FFNN comparators, and the
      Full-sample evaluation mask.
